{"relation": "graphene_layers_from_2D_shape", "applicable": true, "reason": "", "values": {"layer_class": "monolayer", "confidence": "high"}, "source": {"citation": "Ferrari et al. 2006, Phys. Rev. Lett. 97, 187401", "locator": "p. 2 (single sharp 2D peak in graphene, 4 components in bilayer, 2 in bulk graphite) and Fig. 2 of arXiv cond-mat/0606284", "doi": null, "arxiv": "cond-mat/0606284"}, "notes": ["Spectra of more than 5 layers are hardly distinguishable from bulk graphite (Ferrari 2006, p. 2); 3 to 5 layers are not classified by this relation.", "Turbostratic graphite has a single 2D peak with FWHM about 50 cm-1, almost double that of graphene (Ferrari 2006, p. 3); check the width when one component is found."], "provenance": "inferred"}
